    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "An expansive end of terrace period residence extending to c. 215 sq.m set in a mature and private setting on c. 0.5 acre.\n\nLocation\n\n3 Cooldrinagh Terrace is an expansive 4 bed end of terrace period residence with a self-contained 2 bedroom annex, superbly located in the enviably convenient location of Cooldrinagh Lane between Lucan and Leixlip Villages. Set on\na spectacular c. 0.5 acre site, this landmark home elegantly balances historic character with unparalleled adaptability.\nSpanning an impressive 215 sq. m (2,314 sq. ft), the property is currently cleverly configured into three self-contained units—each fully equipped with its own dedicated gas and electricity connections. The accommodation briefly includes 2 kitchens, 3 reception rooms, 4 double bedrooms, 2 bathrooms, and a spacious attached annex provides 2\nadditional bedrooms, a bathroom and a kitchen/dining and living area.\n\nThis property boasts an enormous garden to the rear with huge scope for extending, subject to planning permission.\nThis unique and charming property is a must see for a discerning buyer. This enviably located residence is within\nwalking distance of Leixlip and Lucan Villages, schools, shops, public transport routes, and with a 2-minute drive to the N4, you will be in Dublin City and airport in less than 30 minutes.\n\nThe Property\n\nEntrance Hall: 7.19 m x 3.26 m\nLarge entrance hallway providing access to the living room, dining room, wc and and kitchen with carpet flooring.\n\nKitchen: 3.75 m x 3.3 m\nFully fitted kitchen with base units, linoleum flooring and providing access to the attic.\n\nLiving Room: 4.90 m x 3.14 m\nLarge light filled living room containing brick surrounded fire place, carpet flooring and patio doors providing access to the rear garden.\n\nGuest wc: 2.95 m x 2.00 m\nFully tiled with whb, wc and a tiled floor.\n\nDining Room: 4.93 m x 3.05 m\nWell proportioned reception room featuring carpet flooring and an inset electric fireplace.\n\nLanding: 4.06 m x 0.91 m\nProvides access to all three bedrooms and hot press with carpet flooring.\n\nMaster Bedroom: 4.86 m x 2.82 m\nSpacious bedroom with carpet flooring, overlooking the front\n.\nBedroom 2: 4.23 m x 3.34 m\nOverlooking the front garden with carpet flooring.\n\nBedroom 3: 4.18 m x 2.51 m\nDouble bedroom overlooking the front with carpet flooring.\n\nGarage: 5.41 m x 1.73 m\nProvides direct access to the rear garden.\n\nThe Loft\n\nEntrance Hall: 5.34 m x 0.98 m\nProvides access to the kitchen.\n\nKitchen: 4.71 m x 3.31 m\nLarge kitchen cum dining with wall and base units, tiled splashbacks and tiled flooring.\n\nLiving Room: 4.85 m x 3.15 m\nLarge light filled living room providing access to the bedroom with carpet flooring.\n\nBedroom: 3.68 m x 3.20 m\nSpacious double bedroom with carpet flooring and an en-suite.\n\nEn-suite: 3.08 m x 1.34 m\nPartly tiled with a three piece suite including a mira elite electric shower, wc and whb and tiled flooring.\n\nThe Aviary\nEntrance Hall : 3.07 m x 0.89 m\nProvides access to kitchen / living room, both bedrooms and wc with laminate wood flooring.\n\nKitchen/Living : 4.85 m x 3.27 m\nLight filled kitchen cum living room with wall and base units, tiled splashbacks, laminate flooring and access to the attic.\n\nBedroom 1: 3.62 m x 2.24 m\nSingle bedroom with laminate wood flooring.\n\nBedroom 2: 2.58 m x 2.39 m\nSingle bedroom with laminate wood flooring.\n\nBathroom: 2.87 m x 0.90 m\nWith wc, whb, and large Trition T90s electric shower.\n\nOutside\n\nThe beautiful and expansive rear gardens provide a lovely mixture and trees, herbaceous plants and are punctuated with bursts of every colour. This garden is not overlooked and is perfect for peace of mind if you have young children. There is ample parking to the front of the property.\n\nFeatures\n? c. 2,314 sq. ft / c. 215 sq.m\n? Period home build in 1830s\n? Side entrance\n? Set on c. 0.5 acre on a mature private setting\n? 4 double bedroom and 2 bed self contained annex\n? Spacious and mature rear garden extending to c. 53 metres in length\n? Adjacent to the bus stop providing frequent transport links to Dublin.\n? Opportunity to renovate, convert and develop further\n? 2 minute drive to N4 with easy access to M50\n? Within walking distance to to Leixlip village \n\n\nServices\n? Gas fire central heating\n? Mains water, septic tank, drainage and electricity\n\n\nBER\nExempt"
      },
